## Human Visual System

Light is an electromagnetic spectrum and we (as in humans) are only able to
*perceive* a portion of it; namely 380-780nm. Color is the way our brain
reacts/encodes such information. It could have anything else (maybe perceive
such wavelengths through sound?); doesn't matter. What matters is that color
in reality doesn't exist and only exists through our perception of certain light
wavelengths.

